---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import instance_colour from "../../img/unity/instance-colour.png"
---
<Slide t2="First Look">
    <p class="text-sm-1">We can expose <em>instance variables</em> from a script into Unity's
        editing interface</p>

    <div class="text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="csharp" height="175px">
            { `
public class Colour : MonoBehaviour
{
    public Color colour = new Color(0, 0, 0);
    void Start() { ... }
    void Update() { ... }
}
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ instance_colour }
            alt="Instance: Colour"
            height="300"
            width="500" />
    </div>

    <p class="fragment text-sm-2"><span class="text-red-400 font-bold">NB</span>:
        decide whether you want to use UK or US spelling - and stick to it!</p>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Exercise">
    <ul>
        <li>Update the two-cubes example so that it only needs one script!</li>
        <li>(And see how quickly you can now change the colours.)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>